## Important Product Concepts

### Permanent Access

Permanent Access is designed for unattended devices that need to be available for recurring remote administration. A Getscreen.me Agent is installed and associated with an account, allowing authorized users to connect without requiring the remote user to initiate every session.

### Quick Support

Quick Support is designed for attended, on-demand technical support. It allows technicians to establish one-time remote sessions with end-user devices without permanently adding those devices to Permanent Access.

### Browser-Based Connections

Remote sessions can be initiated and controlled directly from a supported web browser. Technicians do not necessarily need to install a dedicated viewer application on the controlling device.

### Agents

In Getscreen.me documentation and API terminology, software installed on a managed remote device may be referred to as an Agent.

### Teams and Technicians

Business accounts can organize multiple technicians and control access to devices and other resources using team management, departments, and permissions.

### Integrations

Getscreen.me can be integrated into external applications using the HTTP API, connection links, iframe-based sessions, agent deployment, and OEM/white-label capabilities.

## Platforms

Getscreen.me supports remote access workflows across major desktop and mobile platforms, including:

- Windows
- macOS
- Linux
- Android

Remote connections can be controlled from a compatible web browser, allowing the controlling side to operate independently of the operating system in many scenarios.

## Security and Administration

Getscreen.me includes security and administration capabilities for business environments, including access permissions, connection history, audit capabilities, team management, SAML/SSO integration, Active Directory integration, and Self-Hosted deployment options.

Organizations with strict infrastructure, privacy, data residency, or network isolation requirements should evaluate the Self-Hosted edition.

